# Pairs with LivePublisherPinned. The deleted-tree hold retires the pins of a tree
# that is merely soft-deleted, not discarded; recovery then hands the tree back
# with no pins (issue #3930's distinction between Deleted and Discarded).
MODULE: LivePublisherPinnedHoldRetiresRecoverableTree
TARGET: LivePublisherPinned
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the deleted-tree hold retires a recoverable tree's pins
PERTURBS: DiscardRetire

--- FIND
    /\ phase = "discarded"
    /\ \E kc \in Keys \X Cons : pinOff[kc] # NoPin
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a soft-deleted tree is treated as discarded.
    /\ phase \in {"discarded", "deleted"}
    /\ \E kc \in Keys \X Cons : pinOff[kc] # NoPin
--- END
